"""Walk-through of lesson 26, Timeouts & Retries.

Example numbers (mine, checked by script): checkout has 200 threads and serves 100 requests/s; recommendations normally answers in 50 ms
(about 5 busy threads). Slow at 30 s: 100 x 30 = 3,000 threads wanted, the pool is gone in 2 s. A 200 ms timeout (p99.9 is 180 ms): at most 20 busy.
A blip of 1 call in 100: with one retry, both fail 1 in 10,000, so 99% -> 99.99%; calls 800 -> 808 a second (81% of 1,000).
Storm: 3 layers x 3 tries = 27 calls; 40 failing requests/s x 26 extra = 1,040; 800 + 1,040 = 1,840 = 184%. One layer, 3 tries: +80 = 880 = 88%.
Backoff 100/200/400 ms. 1,000 clients on one schedule: three spikes of 1,000 (100, 300, 700 ms); full jitter: busiest 10 ms window about 150 (simulated: 145..179).
Breaker: 5 failures x 200 ms = 1 s; open 30 s x 100/s = 3,000 calls fail at once; threads 100 x 0.05 = 5.
Idempotency: $40 twice = $80. Deadline: 2,000 - 1,700 = 300 ms left; an 800 ms timeout wastes up to 500 ms.
Bulkheads: 40 + 100 + 60 = 200 threads; a 5 s timeout at 100/s wants 500 threads, the 40-thread pool fills in 0.4 s.
"""
